      "writtenOn": "2021-03-22T20:47:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "modules/profile/files/puppetdb/check_puppet_run_changes.py has something similar but for a different use case.\n\nIn general I\u0027m not sure this is the right approach in the long term, but I don\u0027t have a better solution right now.\n\nWhat you could do is to just:\n\n  re.sub(\u0027\\d{4}\u0027, \u0027\u0027, hostname)\n\nThe problem of matching both foo-dev1001 and foo1001-dev, is that both will result in being grouped with \u0027foo-dev\u0027, while probably belonging to two different groups. AFAIK we don\u0027t have this weird case right now, so you might do that anyway, but seems a bit risky IMHO in the longer term, but ok for now.",
      "parentUuid": "c7a09fa9_710b0425",
